From e797fae38c0193c9f04cd03a4763c9faf28fec74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:45:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(langgraph_dev): stop the server when startup is
 interrupted (#534)

start_langgraph_dev() spawns langgraph dev in its own session / process
group, so a terminal Ctrl+C only reaches the CLI, and callers register
their cleanup only after the function returns. A KeyboardInterrupt (or
any other exception) raised after Popen but before the ready return thus
left the server running, together with its PID file and workspace
sidecar, so the next EvoSci deploy hit a port conflict.

Wrap everything after the spawn in try/except BaseException that calls
stop_langgraph_dev(proc) and re-raises. This also covers the existing
"exited immediately" and "not healthy within 60s" paths, which
previously called stop_langgraph_dev themselves.

Closes #534
---
 EvoScientist/langgraph_dev/manager.py | 103 ++++++++++++++------------
 tests/test_langgraph_manager.py       |  73 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)

